@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/sen0401/ch02/diagrams> a owl:Ontology ; rdfs:label "SEN0401 ch02 narrative diagrams - ABox"@en ; owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ; dcterms:identifier "sen0401_ch02_diagrams_abox_v1_0_0" ;
    rdfs:comment "The chapter's authored diagrams as cme:NarrativeDiagram individuals: generated by sen0401_page_data_v2_11_0.py from sen0401_ch02_diagrams_v1_0_0.py, typed by the CME narrative-to-diagram mapping (a module of cme_standards_adoption_v1_3_0.ttl, CME 0.16.0)."@en ; owl:imports <http://example.org/cme/narrative-diagram> .

chx:Diagram_ConstructAndSend a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "From Alice's choice to the network: building and transmitting the transaction"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Workflow ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:ActivityDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 2: Transaction construction (Alice chooses a destination, an amount and a fee; the wallet finds inputs, creates the outputs, attaches the signature), Coin selection (match the payment plus the fee, or generate change), Making change, Transmitting the transaction" ; cme:elementCount 9 ;
    cme:accompanies "Construction" ; cme:accompanies "TransactionConstruction" ; cme:accompanies "CoinSelection" ; cme:accompanies "MakingChange" ; cme:accompanies "Transmission" ; rdfs:comment "the passages describe a procedure with one decision in it - can the chosen inputs match the payment plus the fee exactly, or is a change output needed - from Alice's three choices to the hand-over to the network: a workflow"@en .
chx:Diagram_NetworkRoles a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Who takes part in the network, and what each one does"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:SetOfUses ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:UseCaseDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 2: Who takes part (full verification nodes), Full node (verifies every transaction and block), Lightweight client (block headers only, simplified payment verification), Miner (candidate blocks, proof of work), Mining pool (reward shared in proportion to work), Block explorer (a search engine for the blockchain)" ; cme:elementCount 15 ;
    cme:accompanies "Network" ; cme:accompanies "Participants" ; cme:accompanies "FullNode" ; cme:accompanies "LightweightClient" ; cme:accompanies "Peer" ; cme:accompanies "Miner" ; cme:accompanies "MiningPool" ; cme:accompanies "BlockExplorer" ; rdfs:comment "the passages name the kinds of program on the network and say what each can do and cannot - who does what, not in what order: a set of uses"@en .
chx:Diagram_TransactionOnTheNetwork a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "The life of Alice's transaction, from the memory pool to six confirmations"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:LifeCycle ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:StateDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 2: Transaction propagation, Memory pool (verified but unconfirmed), Unconfirmed transaction, Candidate block, Confirmation (one for the block, one more for each block on top; six is the rule of thumb), Fork and alternative block (two valid blocks at the same height, resolved by the next block), Best blockchain (the most total proof of work)" ; cme:elementCount 14 ;
    cme:accompanies "Propagation" ; cme:accompanies "TransactionPropagation" ; cme:accompanies "Mempool" ; cme:accompanies "Security" ; cme:accompanies "UnconfirmedTransaction" ; cme:accompanies "Confirmation" ; cme:accompanies "AlternativeBlock" ; cme:accompanies "BestBlockchain" ; rdfs:comment "the passages describe the states a transaction passes through after transmission and the events that move it on - received, verified, pooled, in a candidate block, in a block, confirmed, or in a fork that the next block resolves: a life cycle"@en .
chx:Diagram_InvoiceToPayment a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "From Bob's invoice to Bob's confirmation"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Interaction ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:SequenceDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 2: Payment request (Bob's e-commerce system creates a QR code holding an invoice), BIP21 URI (address, amount, label, message), QR code, Transmitting the transaction, Gossiping, Bob's view (the recipient's own check), Confirmation, Block explorer" ; cme:elementCount 13 ;
    cme:accompanies "PaymentRequest" ; cme:accompanies "Bip21Uri" ; cme:accompanies "QrCode" ; cme:accompanies "RecipientVerification" ; rdfs:comment "the passages are an exchange between Bob's store, Alice's wallet, the network's nodes and the miners, in an order that matters - request, scan, transmit, gossip, mine, confirm: an interaction"@en .
chx:Diagram_PartsOfATransaction a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "What a transaction is made of"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:TopicAndParts ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:MindMap ; cme:readFrom "chapter 2, the Transaction part section: inputs (an outpoint - transaction identifier and output index - and a witness), outputs (amount and script), the fee as the difference, size and fee rate, the transaction identifier, serialization, the double-entry ledger image" ; cme:elementCount 16 ;
    cme:accompanies "Transaction" ; cme:accompanies "TransactionPart" ; cme:accompanies "Input" ; cme:accompanies "Output" ; cme:accompanies "UnspentOutput" ; cme:accompanies "Outpoint" ; cme:accompanies "Witness" ; rdfs:comment "the section lists the pieces a transaction is assembled from and the pieces of those pieces - a topic and its parts, laid out to remember"@en .
chx:Diagram_MiningTheBlock a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "How Jing's node turns the memory pool into the next block"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Workflow ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:ActivityDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 2, the Mining section: Miner (Jing's rig and full node), Candidate block (transactions from the memory pool, a commitment to the previous block, no valid proof of work yet), Proof of work (repeated hashing until the header meets the target), Consensus rules (every full node validates the block), Coinbase transaction and Block reward" ; cme:elementCount 9 ;
    cme:accompanies "Mining" ; cme:accompanies "Miner" ; cme:accompanies "CandidateBlock" ; cme:accompanies "ProofOfWork" ; cme:accompanies "ConsensusRules" ; cme:accompanies "CoinbaseTransaction" ; rdfs:comment "the passages describe a repeated procedure with a test and a loop - assemble, hash, check against the target, try again - and what follows when it succeeds: a workflow"@en .
